 "note": "[measured] exploratory, no prereg (owner ruling). Grouped routing is oracle. Same lessons, questions (MANIFEST.sha256 verified) and scorer as the MLX 1B rows; answers folded to one line as in ef0954a.",
 "caveats": "CUDA training is not bit-deterministic: one-10 and group-00 have identical rows and seed yet scored 0.78 vs 0.68 (n=50). peak_mem_gb is GPU memory reserved by torch. Paraphrased set: 1B rewordings that keep repo and command.",
 "license": "Llama 3.2 Community License; Built with Llama",
 "result": "[measured] On the same CUDA trainer at 100 lessons, 3B adapter recall 0.618 vs 1B 0.764 (paraphrased 0.494 vs 0.498); 3B ceiling 0.594 vs 1B 0.238. 1B CUDA adapter 0.764 vs MLX 0.884: the port trains weaker.",
 "follow_up": "[hypothesis] the port gap is non-deterministic GPU kernels or fp32-vs-bf16 LoRA math; a seed repeat at 100 lessons would size the noise before reading 3B < 1B as a model-size effect.",
